# Stage4 package list — one atom per line
# Lines starting with # are ignored
# Edit this file to add or remove packages from the image

# ── Kernel & firmware ──────────────────────────────────────────────
sys-kernel/raspberrypi-sources
sys-boot/raspberrypi-firmware
sys-firmware/raspberrypi-wifi-ucode
dev-embedded/raspberrypi-utils
dev-embedded/rpi-eeprom

# ── RPi 5 hardware ────────────────────────────────────────────────
sys-apps/nvme-cli
sys-block/parted
sys-apps/pciutils
sys-apps/usbutils
sys-apps/i2c-tools

# ── Networking ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
net-misc/networkmanager
net-misc/openssh
net-wireless/wpa_supplicant
net-firewall/iptables
net-firewall/nftables
# net-firewall/firewalld — DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED on this cross-compiled platform
# (2026-08-05, real-build evidence). firewalld is a Python daemon and
# unconditionally needs pygobject -> gobject-introspection -> glib[introspection];
# a scoped glib[introspection] override resolved the depgraph (see the merged
# requested-atoms-resolvable gate history), but the REAL resume build then died in
# glib-2.88.2 src_configure: the ebuild's in-source gobject-introspection
# bootstrap ("work/gobject-introspection-1.86.0-build", ninja) fails under
# cross-emerge — the same failure bc87d1e recorded against glib-2.86, still live
# with the self-testing qemu exe_wrapper eclasses (build log:
# build-pki.rpi5.log 2026-08-05 16:09, 45/52 chain packages built, glib itself
# failed twice). Until the bootstrap cross-compiles, firewalld cannot exist on
# ARM images, and pretending otherwise ships EITHER a silently degraded image
# (the pre-completeness-gate era) or a guaranteed build failure. Host firewalling
# remains: nftables + iptables above, plus the hugmesh-firewall-reconcile OpenRC
# service (Layer-3 backstop, drives nftables directly, owns its own tables).
# Re-adding this atom without a working glib[introspection] cross story will be
# refused by tests/requested-atoms-resolvable.sh — see its rpi5 section.
net-firewall/conntrack-tools
net-misc/socat
# Egress VPN (split-tunnel, fail-closed) — wg-quick (WireGuard, first-class) +
# openvpn (fallback) for the node-level hugmesh-egress-vpn OpenRC service. The
# service is DEFAULT-OFF; the optional-services gate PRUNES these two atoms when
# the egress-VPN service is not selected (see PR6 / gate_optional_services).
net-vpn/wireguard-tools
net-vpn/openvpn
# net-dns/bind-tools — DROPPED: it is now a dummy package that RDEPENDs on the
# full net-dns/bind-9.18 server, which does NOT cross-compile for aarch64 (fails
# src_compile). dig/host are non-essential on a k8s worker (cluster DNS is
# CoreDNS; the node resolves via /etc/resolv.conf). To restore dig-like tooling
# later, prefer net-dns/ldns[drill] (a clean, cross-friendly `drill`) or fix the
# bind cross-build — validate either separately before re-adding here.

# ── System ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
app-admin/sudo
sys-process/cronie
sys-apps/haveged
app-editors/nano
app-misc/screen
dev-embedded/u-boot-tools

# ── Hardened / security (SELinux LSM) ──────────────────────────────
# SELinux is the LSM (hardened/selinux profile). The policy packages'
# pkg_postinst runs the TARGET `semodule`, which can't execute under aarch64
# cross-emerge — so on the Pi the base policy is LOADED AT FIRST BOOT (native)
# by keys-provision; the native x86 build loads it at build time. See SECURITY.md.
sec-policy/selinux-base
sec-policy/selinux-base-policy
sec-policy/selinux-container
sec-policy/selinux-virt
sys-apps/policycoreutils
sys-apps/semodule-utils
sys-apps/checkpolicy
app-admin/setools
sys-libs/libselinux
sys-libs/libseccomp
sys-process/audit

# Container runtime + Kubernetes + their k8s-specific dependencies (containerd,
# kubelet/kubeadm/kubectl, xfsprogs for CSI/PV filesystems, ...) moved to
# packages-k8s.list — appended by build-rpi5-stage4.sh only for cluster-node
# roles (not --role desktop; see ROLE_CLIENT).

# ── Base networking/storage tools (needed by every role, not just k8s) ────
sys-apps/ethtool
sys-apps/iproute2
sys-fs/e2fsprogs
sys-apps/util-linux

# ── KEYS USB provisioning + attached storage + backups ────────────
# jq parses the JSON manifests; dosfstools provides fsck/mkfs for the
# FAT32 KEYS partition; util-linux (above) provides blkid/findfs/wipefs;
# nfs-utils/cifs-utils mount network backup shares.
app-misc/jq
sys-fs/dosfstools
net-fs/nfs-utils
net-fs/cifs-utils
# Encryption-at-rest (LUKS2/dm-crypt) for the attached data partition that backs
# the cluster PVCs / relocated containerd|kubelet|Vault state. The Pi5 has no
# TPM by default, so keys-provision uses the USB-KEYS keyfile (secrets/luks.key)
# as the unlock slot (clevis-tpm2 is enrolled instead on a Pi WITH a TPM HAT).
# See docs/ENCRYPTION-AT-REST.md.
sys-fs/cryptsetup
sys-fs/lvm2

# NOTE: headscale and tailscale are NOT emerged here. They are installed
# as upstream static arm64 binaries by build-rpi5-stage4.sh (the "mesh"
# phase), which avoids overlay/keyword churn. See --skip-mesh / --skip-tailscale.
